    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity users are responsible for bearing deviation electricity costs if they have energy storage or participate in demand-side response during specific periods.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"售电公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Selling companies with distribution network operation rights settle electricity bills with provincial grid enterprises and pay transmission fees according to regulations from government price authorities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power generation enterprises have their deviation electricity recorded by power dispatching institutions, including reasons, start and end times, and volume; their up/down regulation electricity is settled based on declared prices after deducting contract and deviation electricity from actual grid-connected electricity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"风电、光伏发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Wind and photovoltaic power generation enterprises are settled based on actual grid-connected electricity and government-approved prices. In regions with a minimum guaranteed annual utilization hour, the portion within the guaranteed hours is settled at government prices, while excess is handled through market transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Grid enterprises settle deviation electricity costs for non-market users and record cost impacts separately, which are then allocated or returned based on monthly grid-connected electricity ratios.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power trading institutions manage and publish market information, coordinate with power dispatching institutions, and ensure timely, accurate, and complete disclosure of information to all market participants.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power dispatching institutions record deviation electricity for power generation enterprises, monitor market operations, implement risk control measures, and may take market intervention act