    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power trading institution is responsible for organizing electricity transactions, receiving and processing bids, conducting market clearing, submitting results for security verification, and publishing outcomes. It also provides reminders to market participants regarding renewable energy consumption obligations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power dispatching institution provides security constraints for market clearing, conducts security checks on transaction results, and supplies information on available transmission capacity, equipment maintenance schedules, and generation requirements. It plays a key role in ensuring grid safety and stability during all types of transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Market entities include power generation companies, power sales companies, and electricity users who participate in various electricity transactions such as annual, monthly, and intramonth trades. They are required to submit bids, comply with renewable energy consumption responsibilities, and adhere to contract terms.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"可再生能源电力消纳责任主体\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"These are market participants obligated to fulfill renewable energy consumption targets. They must commit to fulfilling these responsibilities when participating in electricity market transactions and are subject to monitoring and reminders by the power trading institution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"关键输电通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"This refers to the available transmission capacity on critical power transmission corridors, which serves as a key constraint in market clearing and security verification processes. The data is provided by the power dispatching institution and used by the trading institution for out-of-market evaluation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"年度（多年）交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Annual (multi-year) transactions involve the trading of electricity volume or hourly electricity for the next year or multiple years. These can be conducted through bilateral negotiation or centralized trading, with pre-confirmation results formed based on annual available transmission capacity.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"月度交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Monthly transactions involve the trading of electricity volume or hourly electricity for the following month. They may also include transactions for remaining months within the year. These are conducted via bilateral negotiation or centralized bidding, with results verified through security checks.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"月内（多日）交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Intra-month (multi-day) transactions cover electricity for remaining days or specific days within a month. These are primarily conducted through centralized trading and can be held regularly or continuously depending on the transaction object.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"偏差电量处理机制\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A category of mechanisms designed to manage deviations between actual power consumption and planned generation. Includes dynamic adjustments before contract execution, pre-marketing for upward/downward regulation, and post-monthly balancing through price-based allocation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电侧上下调预挂牌机制\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A mechanism allowing generators to bid prices for increasing or decreasing output without specifying quantity. Used to adjust supply-demand balance under grid safety constraints, with priority given to energy-saving and low-carbon units.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"偏差电量次月挂牌机制\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A method for handling deviation in electricity supply and demand by adjusting previous month’s actual versus planned generation. Adjustments are made based on declared prices and sorted by cost efficiency, affecting future planned generation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"合同电量滚动调整机制\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A system enabling monthly adjustment of contracted electricity volumes, either through rolling updates for generators or monthly settlement and clearance for users, supporting flexibility in contract execution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全校核\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Security verification is a mandatory process for all electricity transactions, ensuring that proposed trades do not violate grid constraints such as transmission capacity, unit generation limits, or auxiliary service requirements. Conducted by the power dispatching institution and applied at different time scales.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易平台\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The electronic platform where market participants submit bids, receive transaction results, and access information related to electricity trading. It supports all types of transactions and facilitates communication between trading and dispatching institutions.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The power trading institution relies on the power dispatching institution to provide essential security constraints and real-time transmission capacity data necessary for market clearing and safety verification.\"<|>\"information dependency, operational coordination\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"The power trading institution manages all aspects of market participation for market entities, including bid submission, result confirmation, and compliance monitoring, especially regarding renewable energy obligations.\"<|>\"transaction management, regulatory oversight\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"关键输电通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"The power dispatching institution is responsible for providing accurate and updated data on the available transmission capacity of key power corridors, which directly affects transaction feasibility.\"<|>\"data provision, infrastructure constraint\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"年度（多年）交易\"<|>\"关键输电通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"The annual transaction process depends on the annual available transmission capacity provided by the dispatching institution to determine pre-confirmed results and ensure grid security.\"<|>\"capacity constraint, planning accuracy\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"月度交易\"<|>\"关键输电通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"Monthly transaction outcomes are determined based on the monthly available transmission capacity, which is used to conduct market clearing and verify security constraints.\"<|>\"capacity constraint, real-time planning\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"月内（多日）交易\"<|>\"关键输电通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"Intra-month transactions rely on the intra-month available transmission capacity for market clearing and safety validation, ensuring short-term grid stability.\"<|>\"short-term constraint, dynamic adjustment\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"偏差电量处理机制\"<|>\"发电侧上下调预挂牌机制\"<|>\"The upward/downward pre-registration mechanism is one of the core components of the deviation electricity handling system, used to dynamically adjust supply levels during periods of imbalance.\"<|>\"mechanism integration, supply-side response\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"偏差电量处理机制\"<|>\"偏差电量次月挂牌机制\"<|>\"Both mechanisms serve as tools for managing electricity deviations but differ in timing: one operates in advance (pre-registration), while the other adjusts after the fact (next-month registration).\"<|>\"timing difference, complementary functions\"<|>6)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"合同电量滚动调整机制\"<|>\"偏差电量处理机制\"<|>\"The contract rolling adjustment mechanism supports the overall deviation handling framework by allowing flexible contract modifications to reduce execution mismatches.\"<|>\"contract flexibility, deviation mitigation\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"安全校核\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"The power dispatching institution performs the final security verification for all transactions, determining whether they meet grid operational requirements and returning results within specified timeframes.\"<|>\"authority, technical verification\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易平台\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"The power trading institution operates the electronic trading platform, using it to collect bids, publish results, and communicate with market participants throughout the transaction lifecycle.\"<|>\"operational tool, digital interface\"<|>9)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"electricity market mechanism, transaction types, security verification, transmission capacity, deviation management, renewable energy integration\")<|COMPLETE|>"
