    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power dispatching agency is responsible for adjusting long-term trading plans due to grid safety and clean energy absorption, recording reasons, and informing market participants. It also conducts security checks and may implement emergency scheduling based on safety priorities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power trading institution is responsible for receiving contracts, issuing electronic transaction confirmations, publishing settlement basis, tracking and disclosing monthly generation plan progress, and ensuring transparency in contract execution and market operations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The grid enterprise is responsible for installing and maintaining metering devices at designated points, collecting meter data, and settling electricity fees according to government-approved tariffs and physical metered quantities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power generation enterprises are responsible for producing electricity, participating in contracts, and having their electricity volumes settled based on metering data and contractual terms, including handling adjustments during testing periods.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity users are consumers of electricity who pay fees to grid enterprises and may be subject to various pricing mechanisms such as basic rates, time-of-use pricing, and power factor adjustments.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"售电公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power sales companies act as intermediaries between generators and consumers, settle with grid enterprises based on trading institution settlements, and bear financial responsibility for deviations when their contracted users' actual usage differs from planned amounts.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家能源局派出机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The dispatched institution of the National Energy Administration is responsible for receiving post-event reports from the power dispatching agency regarding emergency situations and overseeing compliance with regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"地方政府电力管理部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Local government power management departments receive event reports from the power dispatching agency and participate in oversight of regional electricity market operations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"跨区跨省输电线路\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"Cross-regional and inter-provincial transmission lines are equipped with technical-compliant metering devices at both ends, and settlement points are clearly defined for cross-border transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"产权分界点\"<|>\"geo\"<|>\"The point of property division is where metering devices are generally installed; if not feasible, system losses are accounted for accordingly.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"年度双边交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Annual bilateral trading refers to the process occurring before the start of the annual trading period, during which provincial priority generation electricity is contracted between parties.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"月度交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Monthly trading involves updating and adjusting generation plans based on intra-month (multi-day) transactions and is used to manage deviations in scheduled output.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"多日交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Multi-day trading allows for more frequent adjustments to generation plans and requires specific clearing rules while maintaining monthly settlement.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"紧急情况调度\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Emergency situation dispatching occurs when the power system faces critical conditions, allowing the dispatching agency to prioritize safety and take immediate action.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全校核\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Security checking is a mandatory procedure completed within specified timeframes; failure results in a written explanation by the dispatching agency, published by the trading institution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"优先发电计划\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Priority generation planning includes arrangements for both inter-provincial and local priority electricity, which must be scientifically allocated considering grid safety, supply-demand balance, and power structure.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"基数电量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Base electricity refers to the allocation of power among coal (gas)-fired generation units after deducting priority generation volumes, based on forecasted non-market user consumption.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"保量保价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Guaranteed quantity and price refers to a mechanism under which certain electricity volumes are guaranteed at fixed prices, often applied to priority generation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"保量竞价\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Guaranteed quantity with competitive bidding is a model that promotes participation of priority generation in market mechanisms, increasing the proportion of competitive pricing in inter-provincial transactions.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"The power dispatching agency provides security check results and emergency reports to the power trading institution, which then publishes relevant information to market participants.\"<|>\"information sharing, regulatory compliance\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"The power dispatching agency relies on metering data provided by grid enterprises to determine generation schedules and ensure accurate load balancing.\"<|>\"data dependency, operational coordination\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"The power trading institution receives contracts from power generation enterprises and uses them to form monthly generation plans, which are updated through intra-month trading.\"<|>\"contract processing, planning formation\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"售电公司\"<|>\"The power trading institution issues settlement documents to power sales companies, enabling them to settle with grid enterprises based on agreed-upon terms.\"<|>\"settlement facilitation, contract execution\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"The power trading 