    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"中共中央国务院关于进一步深化电力体制改革的若干意见\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A policy document issued by the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China and the State Council, providing foundational guidance for power system reform, referenced as the basis for establishing the rules on long-term power transactions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家发展改革委\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The National Development and Reform Commission is a key government body responsible for guiding and supervising the implementation of power generation and consumption plan liberalization across regions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家能源局\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The National Energy Administration is responsible for formulating power market planning, market rules, and supervision methods, and oversees regional power markets and trading institutions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力中长期交易基本规则\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A regulatory framework that standardizes long-term electricity trading activities in China, defining market operations, participant roles, and compliance requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity generation enterprises are market participants involved in power production and must comply with trading rules, participate in contracts, and meet technical and environmental standards.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity users are market participants required to engage in market-based transactions, provide demand information, and comply with grid scheduling and energy efficiency regulations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"售电公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power sales companies act as intermediaries between generators and consumers, participating in market trades, managing customer contracts, and fulfilling clean energy consumption responsibilities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电网企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Grid companies ensure safe and stable operation of transmission and distribution networks, provide fair access services, collect tariffs, and support data exchange with power trading platforms.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power trading institutions manage market registration, organize transactions, maintain transaction records, operate the power trading platform, and support market transparency and risk monitoring.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity dispatching agencies are responsible for real-time system balancing, security checks, and providing critical operational data to support market functions.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"储能企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Energy storage enterprises are included as market participants, contributing to grid flexibility and supporting the integration of renewable energy sources.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"计划电量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Planned electricity volume includes priority power generation and base power allocated to coal (gas) units, treated as bilateral transactions between power plants and grids, subject to long-term transaction rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"政府定价的优先发电电量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Electricity generated under government-set prices, which is considered part of planned power and must follow established contractual and settlement procedures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"厂网间双边交易电量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Electricity traded directly between power generation plants and grid companies, forming a subset of planned electricity and governed by long-term transaction rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力辅助服务市场（补偿）机制\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"A separate mechanism for compensating services that support grid stability and reliability, currently not covered under the current rule but to be regulated separately.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"非市场用户\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Users who do not participate in market-based transactions, including those receiving supply at government-fixed prices, such as priority power consumers.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易平台\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"An information system developed and operated by the power trading institution to support market operations, contract management, and data interaction.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"批发交易\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Market transactions involving large-scale electricity purchases and sales among generators, traders, and major users, conducted through bilateral or centralized mechanisms.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"零售交易\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Market transactions where retail customers purchase electricity through power sales companies, typically involving smaller-scale consumption.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"多年、年、季、月、周、多日等电力批发交易\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Long-term electricity trading arrangements covering various timeframes from years down to several days, enabling forward planning and risk management.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力现货交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A type of electricity market operation where electricity is traded for immediate delivery, which may exist in some regions and requires coordination with long-term trading rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"有序放开发用电计划工作\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A policy initiative aimed at gradually opening up power generation and consumption plans, monitored and evaluated by national authorities.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场主体注册\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"The process by which entities such as power generators, users, and retailers formally register to participate in electricity markets, governed by specific procedures.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场准入基本条件\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Standard criteria that all market participants must meet, including legal status, financial independence, creditworthiness, and technical capability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场退出\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"A procedure allowing certain market participants to exit the market under specified conditions, such as non-compliance or termination of contracts.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"中共中央国务院关于进一步深化电力体制改革的若干意见\"<|>\"电力中长期交易基本规则\"<|>\"The basic rules are formulated based on this central policy document and its accompanying files, serving as the foundational legal and policy reference.\"<|>\"policy foundation, regulatory origin\"<|>10)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"国家