    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power trading institution is responsible for processing market registration and deregistration applications, reviewing materials, conducting public announcements, and managing the entire lifecycle of market participants. It also handles disputes, ensures compliance with rules, and maintains historical records for five years.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"国家能源局西北监管局\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The National Energy Administration Northwest Regulatory Bureau is a regulatory body that receives reports and notifications from the power trading institution regarding automatic deregistrations and other significant events, ensuring oversight of market operations.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"省政府电力主管部门\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The provincial government's power management department collaborates with the National Energy Administration Northwest Regulatory Bureau in monitoring and overseeing market activities, particularly in cases involving deregistration or non-compliance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"售电公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A power sales company is a market participant that buys and sells electricity on behalf of customers, required to meet registration conditions, provide services, comply with information disclosure, and fulfill obligations related to renewable energy consumption and contract performance.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"虚拟电厂（含负荷聚合商）\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A virtual power plant, including load aggregators, is a type of new business entity that aggregates distributed resources such as flexible loads and small-scale generation units to participate in the electricity market, initially following guidelines set by the 'Power Sales Company Management Measures'.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"A power generation enterprise is a market participant responsible for producing electricity, adhering to grid dispatching, fulfilling long-term contracts, providing technical data, and complying with market rules and