<|>\"The Power Trading Institution is responsible for organizing market registration, transaction processes, settlement, and information disclosure in accordance with unified standards, and acts as a key operational body within the power market system.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The Power Dispatching Institution manages real-time grid operations and coordinates with the trading institution to ensure reliable and efficient power delivery, playing a critical role in market execution.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电企业\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Power generation enterprises are market participants that produce electricity and engage in medium- and long-term power transactions, subject to registration and compliance with market rules.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"售电公司\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity sales companies act as intermediaries between generators and end-users, offering services such as contract negotiation and market participation on behalf of users.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力用户\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Electricity users, including industrial and commercial entities, participate directly or indirectly in the power market by purchasing electricity through wholesale or retail mechanisms.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"新型独立储能\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"New-type independent energy storage facilities are emerging market participants capable of storing and releasing electricity, contributing to grid flexibility and stability.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"虚拟电厂\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Virtual power plants aggregate distributed energy resources and load flexibility, operating as a single entity in the market, initially regulated under rules similar to those for electricity sales companies.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"智能微电网\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Intelligent microgrids are integrated energy systems combining generation, storage, and load management, capable of operating autonomously or in coordination with the main grid, and can register as unified market participants.\")##\n(\