    "content": "(\"entity\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power dispatching organization is responsible for conducting security checks on various electricity transactions, providing available transmission capacity data, and ensuring grid safety constraints are met. It also plays a role in adjusting generation plans based on grid needs and renewable energy integration.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"The power trading institution manages the submission and processing of market transaction data, conducts market clearing, submits results for security checking, publishes outcomes, handles objections, and consolidates monthly and annual transaction results after security verification.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Market entities include power generation companies, power sales companies, electricity users, and other participants in the electricity market who engage in bilateral or centralized transactions, submit bids, and comply with rules regarding contract execution and adjustments.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"关键通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Key channel available transmission capacity refers to the maximum amount of electricity that can be transmitted through specific transmission lines or paths, used as a constraint in market clearing and security checks.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"安全校核\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Security check is a procedural step required for all types of electricity transactions, conducted by the power dispatching organization within specified timeframes (e.g., 2 working days for monthly, 1 working day for intra-month), to verify whether transactions comply with grid constraints such as transmission capacity, unit generation limits, and auxiliary service requirements.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"月度交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Monthly trading involves the exchange of electricity volume (or hourly electricity) for the next month, or for remaining months of the year, conducted via bilateral negotiation or centralized trading, with pre-transaction submissions and post-clearance security checks.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"月内（多日）交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Intra-month (multi-day) trading focuses on electricity volumes for remaining days or specific dates within the month, primarily conducted through centralized mechanisms but may also use bilateral negotiations, with regular or continuous market openings.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"跨区跨省交易\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"Cross-regional and inter-provincial transactions follow national rules, require coordination with provincial markets, and involve joint planning of transmission schedules and local power balance. They are subject to shared security checks and must adhere to contractual commitments including monthly plans and power curves.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"偏差电量处理机制\"<|>\"event\"<|>\"The deviation electricity handling mechanism allows generators and consumers to adjust their planned output through methods like contract transfer or buyback, especially during periods when actual demand deviates from forecasted generation plans, encouraging use of intra-month trading to minimize discrepancies.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"发电机组\"<|>\"organization\"<|>\"Generation units are power plants or generating facilities capable of providing upward or downward regulation services; they participate in bidding for adjustment services and are ranked based on price and environmental priority during grid balancing.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"政府间协议\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Government-level agreements refer to official contracts between regions or provinces for cross-regional power supply, typically established before the end of the previous year, specifying annual volume, monthly distribution, delivery curves, and pricing, and integrated into priority generation plans.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"优先发电合同\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Priority generation contracts are long-term agreements for government-priced electricity, signed prior to annual bilateral trading, outlining annual volume, monthly breakdown, and pricing, and are given priority in grid scheduling and transmission allocation.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"购售电合同\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"Purchase and sale electricity contracts are formal agreements between buyers and sellers that define key terms such as parties involved, electricity volume, price, execution period, settlement method, deviation measurement, breach of contract liability, and financial details.\")##\n(\"entity\"<|>\"电子交易确认单\"<|>\"category\"<|>\"An electronic transaction confirmation document issued by the power trading institution serves as an executable record equivalent to a paper contract, used as proof of agreement in bilateral and centralized transactions.\")##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"安全校核\"<|>\"The power dispatching organization performs security checks on all transactions, evaluates grid constraints, and returns results within defined timeframes to ensure system stability.\" <|>\"grid security, regulatory compliance\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"安全校核\"<|>\"The power trading institution submits transaction results to the power dispatching organization for security checking and publishes the outcomes after receiving approval.\" <|>\"market process, transaction validation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"月度交易\"<|>\"The power trading institution organizes monthly trading sessions, processes bid submissions, conducts market clearing, and ensures compliance with transmission capacity constraints.\" <|>\"market operations, transaction management\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"月内（多日）交易\"<|>\"The power trading institution facilitates intra-month trading by processing data submissions, performing market clearing, and submitting results for security checks.\" <|>\"short-term trading, dynamic adjustment\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"跨区跨省交易\"<|>\"The power trading institution coordinates cross-regional and inter-provincial transactions, ensures alignment with provincial markets, and manages contractual obligations related to transmission and delivery.\" <|>\"inter-regional coordination, market integration\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"月度交易\"<|>\"Market entities participate in monthly trading by submitting bids or negotiating agreements, which are then processed through the power trading platform and subject to security checks.\" <|>\"market participation, transaction engagement\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"月内（多日）交易\"<|>\"Market entities engage in intra-month trading to adjust their electricity plans, particularly when deviations occur, using either centralized or bilateral methods.\" <|>\"flexibility, real-time adjustment\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"市场主体\"<|>\"偏差电量处理机制\"<|>\"Market entities utilize the deviation handling mechanism to manage mismatches between planned and actual electricity usage through contractual transfers or buybacks, reducing penalties and improving efficiency.\" <|>\"contractual flexibility, risk mitigation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"发电机组\"<|>\"偏差电量处理机制\"<|>\"Generating units participate in the upward and downward regulation mechanisms by submitting bids for adjustment services, enabling them to support grid balance during fluctuations in demand or supply.\" <|>\"grid balancing, ancillary services\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力调度机构\"<|>\"关键通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"The power dispatching organization provides and updates information on key transmission path capacities, which serve as critical constraints in market clearing and security checks.\" <|>\"grid infrastructure, transmission planning\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"电力交易机构\"<|>\"关键通道可用输电容量\"<|>\"The power trading institution uses available transmission capacity data provided by the dispatching organization to conduct market clearing and enforce transaction limits.\" <|>\"market constraint, resource allocation\"<|>8)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"政府间协议\"<|>\"跨区跨省交易\"<|>\"Government inter-agreement forms the foundation for cross-regional and inter-provincial electricity transactions, defining volume, schedule, and pricing to guide market activities.\" <|>\"policy framework, long-term planning\"<|>9)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"优先发电合同\"<|>\"月度交易\"<|>\"Priority generation contracts are incorporated into monthly trading plans and influence the overall generation schedule, ensuring guaranteed output is accounted for before market-based trades.\" <|>\"regulatory priority, generation planning\"<|>7)##\n(\"relationship\"<|>\"购售电合同\"<|>\"电子交易确认单\"<|>\"The electronic transaction confirmation serves as a legally valid substitute for traditional contracts, representing the outcome of successful market transactions.\" <|>\"contract equivalence, digital documentation\"<|>9)##\n(\"content_keywords\"<|>\"electricity market operations, security checking, transaction management, cross-regional trading, deviation handling, grid constraints, market compliance\")<|COMPLETE|>"
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "MANY entities and relationships were missed in the last extraction. Please find only the missing entities and relationships from previous text.\n\n---Remember Steps---\n\n1. Identify all entities. For each identified entity, extract the following information:\n- entity_name: Name of the entity, use same language as input text. If English, capitalized the name\n- entity_type: One of the following types: [organization,person,geo,event,category]\n- entity_description: Provide a comprehensive description of the entity's attributes and activities *based solely on the information present in the input text*. **Do not infer or hallucinate information not explicitly stated.** If the text provides insufficient information to create a comprehensive description, state \"Description not available in text.\"\nFormat each entity as (\"entity\"<|><entity_name><|><entity_type><|><entity_description>)\n\n2. From the entities identified in step 1, identify all pairs of (source_entity, target_entity) that are *clearly related* to each other.\nFor each pair of related entities, extract the following information:\n- source_entity: name of the source entity, as identified in step 1\n- target_entity: name of the target entity, as identified in step 1\n- relationship_description: explanation as to why you think the source entity and the target entity are related to each other\n- relationship_strength: a numeric score indicating strength of the relationship between the source entity and target entity\n- relationship_keywords: one or more high-level key words that summarize the overarching nature of the relationship, focusing on concepts or themes rather than specific details\nFormat each relationship as (\"relationship\"<|><source_entity><|><target_entity><|><relationship_description><|><relationship_keywords><|><relationship_strength>)\n\n3. Identify high-level key words that summarize the main concepts, themes, or topics of the entire text. These should capture the overarching ideas present in the document.\nFormat the content-level key words as (\"content_keywords\"<|><high_level_keywords>)\n\n4. Return output in English as a single list of all the entities and relationships identified in steps 1 and 2. Use **##** as the list delimiter.\n\n5. When finished, output <|COMPLETE|>\n\n---Output---\n\nAdd new entities and relations below using the same format, and do not include entities and relations that have been previously extracted. :"
